{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/docset at 3f635c9170f66dc9a3ca1d35df2a9ac52959e948 on request/docset-citation-integrity.\n\nThe citation gate judges five fatal classes — unresolvable, not an artifact, retired, a path succession cannot maintain, and a commit that is not a full canonical object id — and reports stale without failing, because every artifact at every core package is stale today and failing on stale would redden the set for working as designed.\n\nThe known-failing list bounds the rollout: anything new fails, a changed defect fails, a repaired entry fails so the list must shrink, and now a known citation appearing on a page the list does not cover fails too.\n\nThe loophole this closes was found in review, not by me: the list was keyed on artifact event alone, and declaredActs deduplicates citations across the set, so a new page could cite any known-failing artifact and nothing would change. Each row now carries its exact dependent page set and the comparison includes it; a repeated event row is an error rather than an overwrite.\n\nDemonstrated rather than asserted: adding a known-failing citation to docs/reference/gs/verify.md fails with the page named; the same edit was green before this change.","body":{"branch":"request/docset-citation-integrity","commit":"3f635c9170f66dc9a3ca1d35df2a9ac52959e948","head":"3f635c9170f66dc9a3ca1d35df2a9ac52959e948","path":"internal/docset"}}